                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 3: Generate Building Plan From Assembly shows an example of how to build a BuildingPlan simply as defined by the sequence of Assembly.parts() The inputs for this will require individual customizaiton and definition based on the assembly the User would like to construct. The BuildingPlan is used to define Sequencing, Task Distribution, &amp; Additional information for task completion.

INPUTS:
 - assembly: compas.datastructures.Assembly or compas_timber.assembly.TimberAssembly
   - The assembly you would like to create a building plan from.

- data_type: int
   - The type of geometry from the input assembly
     - 0 == Cylinder (Assembly made of cylinders)
     - 1 == Box (Assembly made of Boxes)
     - 2 == ObjFile (Used for TimberAssemblies &amp;&amp; Mesh)

- robot_keys: list of str
   - A list of assembly keys that are intended to be constructed by the robot.

- prority_lists: list of list of str
   - Priority lists are used to represent parallel tasks.
   - The overall list represents the order in which parts need to be assembled.
   - The internal lists reprepresent parts that can be built in parallel within the overall list</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
